    "course": "C05",
    "seq": 275,
    "acip": "KHA CIG, DE LTAR 'DOD PA DE MI 'THAD PAR THAL, DPAL LDAN CHOS KYI GRAGS PA'I LUNG DANG 'GAL BA'I PHYIR, DER THAL, DE'I GZHUNG LAS, GAL TE DE YANG MTHONG MED LA, , BRTEN NAS GZUGS GZHAN 'BYUNG 'GYUR NA, , ZHES DGRA GNYEN GNYIS KYIS SKYES BU GCIG GI GZUGS LA BLTAS PA DE'I TSE NA, SKYES BU DE'I GZUGS MDZES MI MDZES GNYIS SU GNAS KYANG , GZUGS DE DANG DGRA GNYEN GNYIS KYI BAR DU LAS GZUGS SKYES PAS, DGRA GNYEN GNYIS PO DES GZUGS MDZES MI MDZES GNYIS KA MA MTHONG BA, GRANGS CAN GYIS KHAS BLANGS PA DE 'GOG BYED KYI RIGS PA KHA SPOS PAS KHYOD KYI DE LA GNOD PA'I PHYIR ZER NA,",
    "wylie": "kha cig, de ltar 'dod pa de mi 'thad par thal, dpal ldan chos kyi grags pa'i lung dang 'gal ba'i phyir, der thal, de'i gzhung las, gal te de yang mthong med la, , brten nas gzugs gzhan 'byung 'gyur na, , zhes dgra gnyen gnyis kyis skyes bu gcig gi gzugs la bltas pa de'i tshe na, skyes bu de'i gzugs mdzes mi mdzes gnyis su gnas kyang , gzugs de dang dgra gnyen gnyis kyi bar du las gzugs skyes pas, dgra gnyen gnyis po des gzugs mdzes mi mdzes gnyis ka ma mthong ba, grangs can gyis khas blangs pa de 'gog byed kyi rigs pa kha spos pas khyod kyi de la gnod pa'i phyir zer na",
    "english": "One comes and makes the following claim: Your position, as just explained, is mistaken, for it goes against a statement of the glorious Dharmakirti. This is quite surely the case, for in his major work [entitled The Commentary on Valid Perception] he says, Suppose you say that they don't see it, And circumstances cause another form. What he's talking about here is a belief of the [non- Buddhist] Numerist School. They give the case of a single person whose physical form is looked upon at the same time by his enemy, and also by his friend. In reality, the person's physical form is both attractive and ugly at the same time. Something happens where yet another physical form, one from karma, grows up between the person's true physical form and the enemy and friend looking at it. Because of this neither the enemy nor the friend sees both the attractiveness and the ugliness together. Master Dharmakirti uses logic to refute this concept, and this same logic can be used against the position you have taken, to prove that you are wrong.",
    "raw": "{\"course\": \"C05\", \"acip\": \"KHA CIG, DE LTAR 'DOD PA DE MI 'THAD PAR THAL, DPAL LDAN CHOS KYI GRAGS PA'I LUNG DANG 'GAL BA'I PHYIR, DER THAL, DE'I GZHUNG LAS, GAL TE DE YANG MTHONG MED LA, , BRTEN NAS GZUGS GZHAN 'BYUNG 'GYUR NA, , ZHES DGRA GNYEN GNYIS KYIS SKYES BU GCIG GI GZUGS LA BLTAS PA DE'I TSE NA, SKYES BU DE'I GZUGS MDZES MI MDZES GNYIS SU GNAS KYANG , GZUGS DE DANG DGRA GNYEN GNYIS KYI BAR DU LAS GZUGS SKYES PAS, DGRA GNYEN GNYIS PO DES GZUGS MDZES MI MDZES GNYIS KA MA MTHONG BA, GRANGS CAN GYIS KHAS BLANGS PA DE 'GOG BYED KYI RIGS PA KHA SPOS PAS KHYOD KYI DE LA GNOD PA'I PHYIR ZER NA,\", \"wylie\": \"kha cig, de ltar 'dod pa de mi 'thad par thal, dpal ldan chos kyi grags pa'i lung dang 'gal ba'i phyir, der thal, de'i gzhung las, gal te de yang mthong med la, , brten nas gzugs gzhan 'byung 'gyur na, , zhes dgra gnyen gnyis kyis skyes bu gcig gi gzugs la bltas pa de'i tshe na, skyes bu de'i gzugs mdzes mi mdzes gnyis su gnas kyang , gzugs de dang dgra gnyen gnyis kyi bar du las gzugs skyes pas, dgra gnyen gnyis po des gzugs mdzes mi mdzes gnyis ka ma mthong ba, grangs can gyis khas blangs pa de 'gog byed kyi rigs pa kha spos pas khyod kyi de la gnod pa'i phyir zer na\", \"english\": \"One comes and makes the following claim: Your position, as just explained, is mistaken, for it goes against a statement of the glorious Dharmakirti. This is quite surely the case, for in his major work [entitled The Commentary on Valid Perception] he says, Suppose you say that they don't see it, And circumstances cause another form. What he's talking about here is a belief of the [non- Buddhist] Numerist School. They give the case of a single person whose physical form is looked upon at the same time by his enemy, and also by his friend. In reality, the person's physical form is both attractive and ugly at the same time. Something happens where yet another physical form, one from karma, grows up between the person's true physical form and the enemy and friend looking at it. Because of this neither the enemy nor the friend sees both the attractiveness and the ugliness together. Master Dharmakirti uses logic to refute this concept, and this same logic can be used against the position you have taken, to prove that you are wrong.\"}"
  },
